# A generic, duplicate-safe landing table for events delivered by the Convex component.
#
# The component guarantees AT-LEAST-ONCE delivery: an event Tinybird accepted whose
# acknowledgement never reached the sender is indistinguishable from one never sent, so it is
# sent again. That is a deliberate choice — the alternative loses events rather than
# duplicating them — and it makes the engine here part of the contract rather than a detail.
#
# ReplacingMergeTree keyed on `event_id` collapses repeats. `version` decides which copy wins
# when the same id arrives twice with different contents, so a corrected re-send supersedes the
# original rather than racing it.
#
# The component sends the row VERBATIM: it never adds, renames or drops a column. The host owns
# this schema. The only thing the component requires is that `event_id` equals the envelope's
# `eventId`, because that is what makes a re-send the same row rather than a new one.

SCHEMA >
    `event_id` String `json:$.event_id`,
    `event_type` LowCardinality(String) `json:$.event_type`,
    `occurred_at` DateTime64(3, 'UTC') `json:$.occurred_at`,
    `received_at` DateTime64(3, 'UTC') `json:$.received_at` DEFAULT now64(3),
    `version` UInt32 `json:$.version` DEFAULT 1,
    `payload` String `json:$.payload`

ENGINE "ReplacingMergeTree"
ENGINE_VER "version"
ENGINE_SORTING_KEY "event_id"
ENGINE_PARTITION_KEY "toYYYYMM(occurred_at)"
